# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Almost all configuration now lives in the Google Sheet, not here.
#
#   • Per-client API keys        → the "Workspaces" tab (one row per client)
#   • Slack webhook + global keys → the "Settings" tab (key | value | notes),
#                                   created and seeded automatically on first run
#   • Tuning thresholds          → code defaults in config.py
#
# This file only needs the TWO values that bootstrap reading the Sheet itself.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Required ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Google Sheets document ID (the long string in the URL between /d/ and /edit)
GOOGLE_SHEETS_ID=1aBcDeFgHiJkLmNoPqRsTuVwXyZ0123456789

# HOW to authenticate to that Sheet — pick ONE. The service account (first
# option) is the client-friendly path: no browser, no token refresh.

# Option A (recommended): the full service-account key JSON, on one line.
# Create the service account in Google Cloud, download its key, and share the
# Sheet with its client_email (Editor). In GitHub, paste the JSON straight into
# a secret named GOOGLE_CREDENTIALS_JSON. Locally, either set it here on one line
# or point GOOGLE_CREDENTIALS_JSON_FILE at the downloaded file.
# GOOGLE_CREDENTIALS_JSON={"type":"service_account", ...}
# GOOGLE_CREDENTIALS_JSON_FILE=/path/to/service-account.json

# Option B (legacy): OAuth user token, base64-encoded. Generate locally first:
# run `python monitor.py` once, approve the browser consent (writes token.json),
# then:  base64 -i token.json | tr -d '\n'
# GOOGLE_TOKEN_JSON_B64=

# If none of the above is set, the code looks for credentials.json + token.json
# in the project root and opens a browser on first run (local dev only).

# ── Optional fallbacks (normally set in the Sheet's "Settings" tab) ──────────
# A non-empty Sheet value always wins over these. Keep SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL set as
# a fallback so crash alerts still fire if the Sheet is ever unreadable.

# SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL=https://hooks.slack.com/services/TXXXXXXXX/BXXXXXXXX/XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX
# ZAPMAIL_API_KEY=
# PREMIUMINBOX_API_TOKEN=
# SCALEDMAIL_API_KEY=

# ── Optional (rarely changed) ───────────────────────────────────────────────

# Log verbosity: DEBUG | INFO | WARNING | ERROR
LOG_LEVEL=INFO

# Override provider API base URLs (for tests / mocks) — leave unset in production
# INSTANTLY_BASE_URL=https://api.instantly.ai/api/v2
# ZAPMAIL_API_BASE_URL=https://api.zapmail.ai/api
# PREMIUMINBOX_API_BASE_URL=https://api.premiuminboxes.com/api
# SCALEDMAIL_API_BASE_URL=https://server.scaledmail.com/api/v1
